  "step_3": "The decision reason is about preferring a more right-skewed lottery — one with a greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes. However, in this problem, Lottery A has a high probability (80%) of a favorable outcome (4000 Euros) and only 20% of an unfavorable one (0 Euros), making it left-skewed. Lottery B is certain and thus not skewed. Therefore, neither lottery is right-skewed, so the decision reason does not apply. The verbal report provides no information about skewness, risk, or any evaluation of the distribution of outcomes. The individual's reasoning is entirely missing. Since the individual did not consider skewness or right-skewness at all, and the reason is inapplicable to the problem, the decision reason was not used. The absence of any reference to skewness or unfavorable probability weights confirms this. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason.",
